ult":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":3,"created_at":"2025-05-27T17:22:26Z","updated_at":"2025-06-03T11:54:36Z","closed_at":"2025-06-03T11:48:18Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in 4.3 stable.\n\n### System information\n\nUbuntu LTS\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen you use an animationplayer to control the animationplayer of a 3D gltf character, to add things like melee attack colision boxes, an animationtree will play the tracks, but wont blend the tracks of the gltf file, causing a flickering issue.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nCreate a 3D character gltf character.\nCreate a new AnimationPlayer and then add the gltf animations as tracks.\nCreate an AnimationTree to control this new AnimationPlayer.\nMake a Blend2D node to blend between the walk and idle state.\nSet up Continuous mode to blend.\n\nIssue can be fixed with using the non continous blending mode, but the animationplayer will snap to separate animations and wont blend them.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/66fca683-7ee5-4a09-bd5f-071d8786bec1\n\n[Bug.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/20463713/Bug.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tokag